            apTip: "The AP Lit exam's highest-scoring essays often demonstrate exactly this kind of sophisticated INTEGRATION — showing how MULTIPLE literary elements (not just one in isolation) work together to develop a cohesive, well-supported thematic argument — while still maintaining a clear, focused analytical through-line (the central thematic claim) connecting all the specific textual evidence discussed."
