            wrong: { 0: "The most sophisticated, highly-scored literary essays typically engage with genuine COMPLEXITY and NUANCE, rather than settling for the SIMPLEST, most obvious possible claim — a stronger thesis specifically captures the interpretive richness/complexity the text actually offers.", 2: "While literary texts ARE genuinely complex, this does NOT mean defensible arguments cannot be constructed about them — sophisticated literary analysis SPECIFICALLY involves building well-EVIDENCED, defensible interpretive arguments, even about complex, nuanced texts; complexity doesn't preclude argumentation, it enriches it.", 3: "A strong literary essay should reflect the WRITER'S OWN original analytical thinking and interpretation (developed through the writer's own close reading and textual evidence), not simply RESTATE someone else's previously published critical interpretation without original contribution." },
